            "title": "Applicable",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "source_vocabulary",
          "source_state",
          "canonical_state"
        ],
        "title": "ProcessIRAuthoringStateMappingV1",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ProcessIRDocumentSemanticsV1": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "What a node does to the document stream.\n\nThe three questions a caller must answer to place a node correctly: does it\nneed documents arriving, what does it leave behind, and does it act per\ndocument or per group. ``stream_replacing`` is called out separately from\n``documents`` because a node that REPLACES the stream discards what came\nbefore it, which is how a per-document property silently stops existing.",
        "properties": {
          "input_documents": {
            "enum": [
              "none",
              "optional",
              "required"
            ],
            "title": "Input Documents",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "output_documents": {
            "enum": [
              "none",
              "documents",
              "stream_replacing",
              "consumed"
            ],
            "title": "Output Documents",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "grouping": {
            "enum": [
              "per_document",
              "per_batch",
              "all_documents",
              "not_applicable",
              "unspecified"
            ],
            "title": "Grouping",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "input_documents",
          "output_documents",
          "grouping"
        ],
        "title": "ProcessIRDocumentSemanticsV1",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "One bounded page of the authoring contract.\n\n``catalog_entry_count`` (everything), ``matched_entry_count`` (everything\nthe filter selected) and ``returned_entry_count`` (what is in this page) are\nthree different numbers and all three are published. A caller who sees only\nthe third cannot tell a narrow filter from a truncated page.\n\nThe two ``unlisted_*_state`` fields publish the ALLOWLIST RULE once. The\nunderlying registries are closed \u2014 a placement or a connector action that is\nnot listed is rejected \u2014 so enumerating the complement would mean shipping a\ncombinatorial table that silently goes wrong every time a node kind is\nadded. One field states the rule instead.",
